{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"repeating decimal repeating decimal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","fileName":"Repeating Decimal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Repeating Decimal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Fractions and Decimal Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Rational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"repeating decimal repeating decimal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","fileName":"Repeating Decimal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Repeating Decimal","heading":"Repeating Decimal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A repeating decimal has a finite block of digits that continues indefinitely, such as\n\n$$0.090909\\ldots=0.\\overline{09}.$$\n\nEvery repeating decimal is a [[Rational Number]]. To convert one to a fraction, let a variable equal the decimal, multiply by powers of ten until two forms share the same infinite tail, and subtract. For (x=0.\\overline{09}), (100x-x=9), so (99x=9) and (x=1/11). A terminating decimal is also rational because trailing zeros make it a repeating form.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Rational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"repeating decimal repeating decimal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Repeating Decimal.md","fileName":"Repeating Decimal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Repeating Decimal","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Rational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}